# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "The two-qubit gate {#the-two-qubit-gate}"
msgstr "Dvoukubitové hradlo {#the-two-qubit-gate}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Every bond $(i, j)$ of the lattice gets the same two-qubit gate, made of a Heisenberg entangler followed by random fields:\n"
msgstr "Každá vazba $(i, j)$ mřížky dostane stejné dvoukubitové hradlo, složené z Heisenbergova entangleru následovaného náhodnými poli:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Large\n"
"U_{ij} =  e^{iJ(X_iX_j + Y_iY_j + Z_iZ_j)}\\; e^{i(h_i Z_i + h_j Z_j)}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Large\n"
"U_{ij} =  e^{iJ(X_iX_j + Y_iY_j + Z_iZ_j)}\\; e^{i(h_i Z_i + h_j Z_j)}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "with $h$ drawn uniformly from $[-\\pi/2, \\pi/2]$ for every gate.\n"
msgstr "kde $h$ je pro každé hradlo taženo rovnoměrně z $[-\\pi/2, \\pi/2]$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "> **Question.** How would you decompose $U_{ij}$ into gates the hardware can run?\n"
msgstr "> **Question.** Jak bys rozložil(a) $U_{ij}$ na hradla, která hardware dokáže provést?\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Answer\">\n"
msgstr ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Odpověď\">\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**The fields** are easy. $e^{ihZ}$ is a single-qubit rotation $R_Z(-2h)$ on each qubit.\n"
msgstr "**Pole** jsou snadná. $e^{ihZ}$ je jednokubitová rotace $R_Z(-2h)$ na každém kubitu.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**The entangler** is the hard part. $XX$, $YY$ and $ZZ$ commute, so it factors into three rotations, $R_{XX}$, $R_{YY}$ and $R_{ZZ}$. Each takes two CNOTs, which makes six CNOTs per gate.\n"
msgstr "**Entangler** je těžší část. $XX$, $YY$ a $ZZ$ komutují, takže se rozloží na tři rotace, $R_{XX}$, $R_{YY}$ a $R_{ZZ}$. Každá vyžaduje dvě hradla CNOT, což dává šest CNOT na hradlo.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "There is a better way. Any two-qubit gate can be built from at most three CNOTs and single-qubit rotations. The optimal circuit starts from the form $e^{i(aXX + bYY + cZZ)}$, and this entangler already has that form with $a = b = c = J$. So it maps straight onto three CNOTs, and the single-qubit angles are linear in $J$. The experiment code builds the gate this way.\n"
msgstr "Existuje lepší způsob. Každé dvoukubitové hradlo lze sestavit nejvýše ze tří CNOT a jednokubitových rotací. Optimální obvod vychází z tvaru $e^{i(aXX + bYY + cZZ)}$ a tento entangler už tento tvar má s $a = b = c = J$. Mapuje se tedy přímo na tři CNOT a jednokubitové úhly jsou lineární v $J$. Kód experimentu sestavuje hradlo tímto způsobem.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "On hardware, every two-qubit gate adds noise, so halving the CNOT count matters.\n"
msgstr "Na hardwaru každé dvoukubitové hradlo přidává šum, takže na snížení počtu CNOT na polovinu záleží.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
msgstr ""

